>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `CS_AESOP_SAFE_TAC`

``` hol4
aesopLib.CS_AESOP_SAFE_TAC :
  aesopLib.aesop_config ->
  clasetLib.claset -> simpLib.simpset -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constructs the context-explicit, configurable form of `AESOP_SAFE_TAC`.

`CS_AESOP_SAFE_TAC config cs ss` normalises and safely saturates with the
supplied claset and simpset. It leaves the exact safe frontier and tries no
unsafe rules. `config.max_depth` bounds branch depth and normalisation.
Both configuration fields must be non-negative; `max_rapps` is relevant
only to the unsafe search performed by `CS_AESOP_TAC`.

The tactic processes no theorem list. The caller is responsible for
inserting facts and adding temporary rules or rewrites to `cs` and `ss`.
Persistent split rules and session tactic rules registered by
`augment_aesop` remain part of the Aesop rule sources.

The tactic succeeds only when the goal state changes.

### Failure

Fails if safe saturation leaves the goal unchanged, if a depth or
normalisation limit is reached, or if either configuration field is
negative.

### Example

``` hol4
val safe_aesop =
  aesopLib.CS_AESOP_SAFE_TAC aesopLib.default_config
    (clasetLib.the_claset ()) (bossLib.srw_ss ());
```

